  "abstract": "Tests whether a discrete entropic gravity operator with MOND-like infrared enhancement remains compatible with cosmological structure growth when its transition scale is \u039b-locked. Embeds a scale-dependent Geff(k) into the linear growth equation and compares \u039b-locked (super-Hubble) versus sub-Hubble transition scales. Finds that only \u039b-locking (L\u039b \u2273 H0\u22121) preserves realistic \u03c38 \u2248 0.81; sub-Hubble transitions cause catastrophic overgrowth.",
